			<div class="content" id="post-content-754924">
									

<p>I like this one, although I have a feeling its going to be downvoted into oblivion because people are going to get all uppity about it in the same vein as Leicontis appears to be. On the internet, it's the atheists and agnostics are the Jack Chicks, so its not unexpected, but still a shame.</p>
<p>To avoid having the non-religious people on this site turn into <a href="http://reilly2040.co.uk/blog/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/redlanterns.jpg">Red Lanterns</a> over it, I recommend that the descriptions be altered to be similar to the ones for the final one, with a Rational Route of Infection and a Spiritual Route Of Infection. Leicontis misread it; because it doesn't say that highly religious people are very smart. It's an Or Gate; either you're really smart or a devout believer that causes that facet of infection.</p>
<p>For example, I'd write out the first infection route as something like this:</p>
<p><em>Subjects described by others as self-centered or cowardly, or self-identified as religious agnostics…</em></p>
<p>I don't know why I bother making these suggestions because, like I said, never doubt the ability for someone who isn't spiritual to get <em>really</em> miffed when people talk about them in a less-than-pleasant fashion.</p>

